FYI, this change causes false positives when `for`/`while` loops are used in functional components, see https://github.com/facebook/react/issues/31687

Example of code that now gets (incorrectly) flagged by this rule:

```ts
const MyComponent = () => {
  const [state, setState] = useState(0);

  for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    console.log(i);
  }

  return <div></div>;
};
```

